{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No-fault eviction relocation and LAHD declaration filing (RSO/JCO)","requirement":"Before evicting an RSO or JCO tenant for a no-fault reason, a landlord must pay relocation assistance and file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD; the notice may be served only after filing and a copy filed within 3 days.","key_value":"Relocation assistance per unit; notice copy filed within 3 days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants evicted without fault from rental units covered by the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":"Resident manager evicted to be replaced by another resident manager; eviction required by hazardous conditions caused by a natural disaster not due to landlord negligence; landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against relocation assistance.","penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration with LAHD makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO; a tenant may raise non-payment of relocation assistance as an affirmative defense or pursue a private right of action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC §§ 151.09, 165.03","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":"Landlords displacing tenants by demolition for new construction must pay the higher of City RSO/JCO amounts or State Housing Crisis Act amounts.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO relocation assistance amounts, July 2026 - June 2027","requirement":"Landlords displacing tenants for a no-fault reason must pay per-unit relocation assistance of $11,000 to an eligible tenant with under three years' tenancy and $14,400 at three years or more; qualified tenants receive $23,150 and $27,400.","key_value":"$11,000 / $14,400 eligible; $23,150 / $27,400 qualified; July 1, 2026 to June 30, 2027","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced for a no-fault reason under the RSO or JCO; the amounts are paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":"Does not apply where a Protected Unit is demolished for new construction and the tenant is lower income (80% AMI or lower).","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"A. Relocation Assistance Bulletin, Chart A","quoted_span":"CHART A: RSO or JCO Amounts for Households Above Low Income Effective July 1, 2026 through June 30, 2027 * Household Type Tenancy Length Less than 3 Years Tenancy Length 3 Years or More Eligible Tenant $11,000 $14,400 Qualified Tenant $23,150 $27,400","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deadline to provide relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord must make relocation assistance available within 15 days of serving the written notice of eviction; at the landlord's discretion and cost the funds may instead be placed in an escrow account within that same period.","key_value":"Within 15 days of service of the notice","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced for a no-fault reason from RSO- or JCO-covered rental units in the City of Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"RAC Regulations § 960.00","quoted_span":"Payment shall be made available within fifteen (15) days of service of the written notice of eviction","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"One month's rent relocation for single-family dwellings (JCO)","requirement":"For a JCO-covered single-family dwelling, relocation assistance owed by an owner who is a natural person is one month's rent in effect when the notice to terminate was served, as money or credit.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Single-family dwelling subject to the JCO owned by a natural person, including a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Owner owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles"},"exemptions":"LAMC Section 151.30(E) shall not apply.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 165.06","quoted_span":"When the residential real property is a single-family dwelling subject to the JCO and the owner is a natural person, including natural persons who hold properties in a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that natural person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles: one month's rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation options and penalties","requirement":"An owner who demolishes a Protected Unit for new construction within 5 years after filing a Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict must follow RPO relocation requirements, choosing one of three options and paying the highest applicable amount.","key_value":"3 relocation options; penalties from $250,000 per displaced unit","coverage_conditions":"Protected Units demolished for the purpose of new construction within 5 years after filing of the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD; all RSO units are Protected Units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Protected Units as defined by the RPO, including all RSO units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","citation":"L.A. Ordinances #188481 and #188482","quoted_span":"Owners who demolish a Protected Unit for the purpose of new construction within 5 years after the filing of the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD are required to comply with relocation requirements under the RPO. Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owners must pay the highest of the applicable State Housing Crisis Act or City RSO/JCO relocation amounts.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Reduced relocation assistance for mom-and-pop properties","requirement":"A landlord of a building with four or fewer rental units may pay reduced relocation assistance for a good-faith eviction for occupancy by the owner, an eligible relative or a resident manager if the conditions of LAMC Section 151.30 are met.","key_value":"Reduced relocation assistance","coverage_conditions":"Buildings with four or fewer rental units; landlord has not used this provision in the previous three years; landlord owns no more than four residential units; the eligible relative owns no residential property in the City of Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Reduced payment only for evictions for occupancy by the owner, an eligible relative or a resident manager"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 151.30","quoted_span":"Mom and Pop properties may pay reduced relocation assistance payments to their tenants for a good faith eviction for occupancy by the owner or eligible relative, provided that requirements in Section 151.30 of the LAMC are met.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
